I walk through the market.
It is very crowded there.
I see a large vegetable stall.
There are nice red tomatoes there.
I point to those tomatoes.
"Brother, what is the price for one kilo of tomatoes?" I ask.
"Forty rupees," the vendor says.
I nod my head.
I select a few large tomatoes.
I give them to him.
"Please weigh this," I say.
He puts the tomatoes on the scale.
"It is half a kilo," he says.
"That will be twenty rupees."
I give twenty rupees.
He puts the tomatoes in my cloth bag.
I say thanks.
I go to the next shop.
